    "created_at": "2025-06-04T14:04:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-04T14:04:53Z",
    "body": "Isn't the idea that `setHTML()` doesn't go through TT because it guarantees unsafe bits have been removed? If there are other places where you would use the output of `createHTML` we should probably introduce equivalent methods. (I proposed `prependHTML()` and such in the past.)",
