    "created_at": "2025-06-05T12:11:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-05T12:11:34Z",
    "body": "+1 to what @annevk says: `setHTML()` is not going to be controlled by TT because it guarantees XSS-safety.\n\nIf people want to plug their _own_ sanitizer into TT, they will currently have to `setHTML` + get again, which causes a parsing roundtip and that is said. We might want to look at the Sanitizer doing string-based inputs as a v2 thing",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
